  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In case of noble gases, Vander waal forces exist between atoms which are directly proportional to size of elements.</p><p>Due to bigger size of Xe, it&#39;s electron cloud gets polarized more and as a result it has stronger Van Der Waals forces leading to a higher boiling point.</p>"
